                <pb facs="0264" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.1211/242</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Confidential Agent of the Provisional Government
                        of Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Díaz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May 20,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to advise your
                    Excellency that I have been named by Don Adolfo de la Huerta, president of the
                    Provisional <pb facs="0265" n="165" xml:id="pg165"/> Government of Mexico, as
                    confidential agent of that government, at Washington, charged with its
                    representation near the government of the United States, to succeed General
                    Salvador Alvarado, who has been appointed Secretary of the Department of
                    Finance.</p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvaro Torre Díaz</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
